--- Beehtrix 2026-10-28T06:32:03Z
@evisdren I traced #412 (and #534, which looks like the same thing) to compact `transcript.jsonl` records (the v:1 shape, with content at the top level instead of under `message`) not being read by the history and conversation readers, so a default `refresh` gives 0 records and 0 exchanges. Distill got the same fallback in #264. I have a fix with tests that fail on main for Claude Code, Codex and Pi, and it also handles the upgrade path by invalidating old scan caches. Would you like a PR for this? I can open it against `entire-brain` right away. I've kept #411's `verify` change separate, pending your answer there.


--- Beehtrix 2026-10-29T01:54:37Z
@evisdren update: I opened https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/560 for this. It's rebased on your #557 and now covers only what's left: mining tool output for code facts, rebuilding stale history indexes after upgrade, and one shared helper. Happy to narrow or close it if you'd rather handle it another way.

